Group 2 -  Diagnostic Evidence Team (DET)
 Member 1 (Pediatric Pathologist (Lead)): Analyzes kidney biopsy specimens and provides critical histological evaluations for conditions related to recurrent UTIs and renal damage, focusing on potential findings such as interstitial nephritis or chronic changes.
 Member 2 (Infectious Disease Specialist): Offers insight into potential infectious causes of recurrent UTIs and any secondary renal implications, advising on the management of antibiotic therapies.
 Member 3 (Pediatric Immunologist): Evaluates any underlying immunological factors contributing to recurrent infections, suggesting potential tests and treatments for enhancing the child's immune response.

Group 3 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
 Member 1 (Senior Pediatric Nephrologist (Lead)): Provides overall expertise as the final reviewer of all diagnostic findings and treatment approaches to address the child's recurrent UTIs and related renal pathology.
 Member 2 (Pediatric Urologist): Collaborates in discussing the need for possible surgical interventions based on the findings from the IAT and DET, ensuring all options are considered.
